#HELPS

0 ADVANCE WOLFPROGRESSION~
Syntax: advance
Werewolves start at rank 1 and can advance themselves through rank 4.
The current rank requires 20 times that rank in completed quests and
1000 times that rank in lifetime mob kills. These counters are checked,
not spent. The old Gnosis/Rage and 500-kill requirements are obsolete.
ADVANCE cannot award rank 5; it is not a self-service mastery shortcut.
Related: RANKS, TRIBEGIFTS, WWGIFTS, WWPOWERS.
~

0 TRIBEGIFTS WOLFGIFTCHOICE~
Syntax: tribegifts
        tribegifts <breed, auspice or tribe name>
Displays or selects your preferred breed, auspice and tribe.
Each of the three choices can be made once; this command cannot replace
an already selected preference. Use the full name without quotation
marks, for example TRIBEGIFTS BLACK FURIES.
A preferred track can reach 5; other tracks in its category cap at 4.
Selecting a preference does not itself buy every gift rank.
Related: WWGIFTS, BREEDS, AUSPICES, TRIBES.
~

0 GIFTS WWGIFTS WOLFGIFTTRAINING~
Syntax for Werewolves: gifts
                       gifts <full track name>
WWGIFTS is an alias for the Werewolf gift trainer.
With no argument it displays breed, auspice and tribe ratings.
With a full track name it buys the next rank using primal: 10 times
the next rank for a preferred track, or 15 times for other tracks.
Preferred tracks cap at 5; other tracks cap at 4, not 3.
Example: GIFTS CHILDREN OF GAIA. Do not quote the multiword name.
Other parent classes may have their own class-specific gift menus.
Related: TRIBEGIFTS, WWPOWERS.
~

0 WWPOWERS WOLFCOMMANDS~
Syntax: wwpowers
Lists the Werewolf command powers unlocked by current gift ratings.
This is an information menu, not a trainer or a grant-all command.
Use WWGIFTS to train and WWUPKEEP to inspect active powers.
The individual command help pages give the actual handler requirements;
older tribe lore and menu labels are not extra, separate abilities.
~

0 PERSUASION JAMTECH RESHAPEOBJECT HOMIDCOMMANDS~
Homid command gifts:
  1 PERSUASION: toggles the native awe/persuasion flag.
  2 JAMTECH <target>: attempts to disrupt an opponent's weapon.
  3 RESHAPEOBJECT <carried object> RENAME <short description>
    RESHAPEOBJECT <carried object> KEYWORD <extra keywords>
    RESHAPEOBJECT <carried object> FLAGS <glow|hum>
Reshaping requires eligible, quest-owned equipment and does not create
an artifact or copy combat enchantments.
Homid 4 DISQUIET and Homid 5 WARD have separate help entries.
~

0 PRIMALANGER BURROW PORCUPINE METISCOMMANDS~
Metis command gifts:
  1 PRIMALANGER: trades pain for rage; not a healing spell.
  2 BURROW: toggles native earthmelding, with its normal restrictions.
  4 PORCUPINE: toggles the bristles flag that obstructs embraces.
Metis 3 uses NIGHTSIGHT; Metis 5 TOTEMGIFT has its own help entry.
These are individual toggles, not permanent grants of every Metis gift.
~

0 BEASTLIFE LUPUSCOMMANDS WOLFELEMENTAL~
Syntax: beastlife
Requires Lupus 4 and toggles the native animal-master flag.
Lupus also supplies HEIGHTEN at 1, SCRY at 2 and automatic balance
benefits. Lupus 5 uses ELEMENTAL <fire|water|earth|air> <target>.
The Werewolf ELEMENTAL command is not the Elemental parent's trainer.
Related: LUPUS, HEIGHTEN, SCRY, ELEMENTAL.
~

0 BLUR BLISSFUL WHELP RAGABASHCOMMANDS~
Ragabash command gifts:
  1 BLUR: toggles native Blur concealment.
  2 BLISSFUL: toggles Blissful Ignorance concealment.
  4 WHELP <target>: applies a temporary hit, damage and armor penalty
    when the native attack checks succeed.
Using one concealment command does not train the other gift ranks.
Related: RAGABASH, WWGIFTS, WWUPKEEP.
~

0 MOTHER PULSE GRASP LOBOTOMY THEURGECOMMANDS~
Theurge command gifts:
  1 MOTHER <target>: heals an eligible target; self-healing requires 2.
  3 PULSE: toggles spirit/shadow sight.
  4 GRASP <target>: draws the caster and eligible target into the Umbra.
  5 LOBOTOMY <target>: drains mana, bounded at zero.
Mother's healing is capped at the target's maximum health.
These commands retain their native target, ward and combat checks.
~

0 WALLGRANITE GEAS PHILODOXCOMMANDS~
Philodox command gifts:
  4 WALLGRANITE <direction>: creates native granite-wall/portal
    obstruction for a valid exit; do not expect to overwrite any exit.
  5 GEAS <target>: attempts the native charm/follower effect on an
    eligible creature, subject to its existing resistance checks.
Philodox 2 STRENGTHOFPURPOSE has a separate restored-power help entry.
Related: PHILODOX, WWGIFTS, STRENGTHOFPURPOSE.
~

0 WYLD WYRMCALL SONGOFRAGE GALLIARDCOMMANDS~
Galliard command gifts:
  1 WYLD: broadcasts a Werewolf assistance call while fighting or
    critically wounded; it does not summon an automatic army.
  3 WYRMCALL: attempts to reveal concealed creatures in the room.
  4 SONGofRAGE <target>: provokes or increases eligible targets' rage.
  5 BRIDGEWALK <target>: see BRIDGEWALK for travel and misfires.
The command name is SONGofRAGE, entered as one word.
~

0 BRIDGEWALK MOONBRIDGE~
Syntax: bridgewalk <target>
Requires Galliard 5, not Ragabash 5. The target must be an eligible
visible creature elsewhere; players must permit summoning.
Both rooms must permit travel. Combat/timers, restraint, curses/webs,
roots, private/solitary rooms and incompatible planes prevent travel.
An otherwise valid attempt has a one-in-three moon fluctuation:
it tries a limited number of random destinations in the legacy room
range 100..16000. If none is found, it fails without moving you.
Random landings exclude safe/private/solitary/no-recall/no-teleport
rooms. A permitted landing is not a promise of freedom from enemies.
Invalid requests do not send you elsewhere or dismiss Blissful Ignorance.
~

0 HELIOS AHROUNCOMMANDS~
Syntax: helios
Requires Ahroun 5 and toggles the native Helios/solar-protection flag.
It is separate from HALOSUN and does not change your tribe selection.
Ahroun 1 RAZORCLAWS has its own restored-power help entry.
Related: AHROUN, RAZORCLAWS, WWUPKEEP.
~

0 BREATHWYLD AEOLUS FOG BODYWRACK BLACKFURYCOMMANDS~
Black Furies command gifts:
  1 BREATHWYLD: restores the caster's health, capped at maximum.
  2 AEOLUS or FOG: outdoors-only world-fog toggle, with the native
    60-second weather cooldown.
  5 BODYWRACK <target>: attempts the native damaging attack.
BODYWRACK requires 5, not the rank 4 in older lore.
The restored WYLDWARP power has a separate help entry.
~

0 FRIEND INFEST BONEGNAWERCOMMANDS~
Bone Gnawer command gifts:
  3 FRIEND <target>: transfers some of your rage to an eligible target.
  4 INFEST: summons the native charmed infestation helper.
Friend consumes rage you actually have; it is not a free rage refill.
The helper uses the game's normal follower and charm mechanisms.
Related: WWGIFTS, WWUPKEEP.
~

0 DAZZLE HALOSUN CHILDRENOFGAIACOMMANDS~
Children of Gaia command gifts:
  3 DAZZLE <target>: attempts to disrupt the eligible target's actions.
  5 HALOSUN: toggles the native sunshield item-affect flag.
DAZZLE requires 3, not the rank 2 in older lore.
Other shared powers include CALM, SPIRITGUARDIAN and STRIKETHEAIR;
use their own help and actual command gates rather than old menu names.
~

0 FAERIELIGHT HOWLBANSHEE BALORSGAZE FIANNACOMMANDS~
Fianna command gifts:
  1 FAERIELIGHT: creates a native light-ball object.
  2 HOWLBANSHEE: attempts a room-wide fear/disruption howl.
  5 BALORSGAZE <target>: applies the native Balor's Gaze attack.
BALORSGAZE requires 5, not the rank 4 in older lore.
Fianna's illusion commands share the native illusion system; they are
not permission to impersonate staff or bypass target protections.
Related: ILLUSIONARYFORM, CLONEOBJECT.
~

0 DIAGNOSTICS SURGE DOPPLEGANGER SUMMONNETSPIDER GLASSWALKERCOMMANDS~
Glass Walker command gifts:
  1 DIAGNOSTICS <carried object>: inspects the selected item.
  3 SURGE: attacks eligible non-group opponents in the room.
  4 DOPPLEGANGER <target>: adopts the native appearance disguise.
  5 SUMMONNETSPIDER: summons the native charmed net-spider helper.
Surge retains native safety/PK checks and does not attack your group.
Disguise is not a change of account name, class or staff permissions.
~

0 CLAPTHUNDER PARALYZINGSTARE DOMINATOR OBEDIENCE SHADOWLORDCOMMANDS~
Shadow Lord command gifts:
  2 CLAPTHUNDER: native room thunder attack, not an automatic passive.
  3 PARALYZINGSTARE <target>: attempts to interrupt the target.
  4 DOMINATOR <target>: steals eligible targets' rage/blood energy.
  5 OBEDIENCE <target|all> <command>: attempts native domination.
Obedience uses the restricted domination-action checks; it is not a
general FORCE command and cannot grant administrative permissions.
The former rank-4 Open Wounds placeholder is not a separate command.
~

0 REACH SILENTSTRIDERCOMMANDS~
Syntax: reach <target>
Requires Silent Striders 5. Attempts to pull an eligible nearby target
out of the native shadow plane, subject to its normal ward checks.
It does not teleport you to an arbitrary room or change your account
class. Other Silent Strider advantages are native passive benefits.
~

0 WRATH MASTERY SILVERFANGCOMMANDS~
Silver Fang command gifts:
  3 WRATH: applies the native fear/hit/damage penalty attack.
  5 MASTERY <Garou> <command>: attempts to command an eligible Garou.
MASTERY requires 5, not the rank 4 in older lore.
Mastery uses restricted command checks, not unrestricted staff FORCE.
Related: SHIELD, SILVER FANGS, WWGIFTS.
~

0 FALLING STARGAZERCOMMANDS~
Syntax: falling <target>
Requires Stargazers 1. Performs the native Falling Touch attack,
including damage and action delay when its checks succeed.
Higher gift ranks scale the existing attack; this is not a separate
ability to train at each rank.
~

0 INVISIBILITY FETISHDOLL UKTENACOMMANDS~
Uktena command gifts:
  4 INVISIBILITY: invokes the native invisibility effect.
  5 FETISHDOLL <player>: consumes a matching body part held in your
    hand and creates that online player's native voodoo doll.
The body part's type and recorded name must match the player.
NPCs are not valid doll targets. A missing doll template does not
consume the component. Use FETISHDOLL, not the old shortened FETISH label.
Related: SHROUD, UKTENA, WWGIFTS.
~

0 CAMOUFLAGE CUTTING BLOODYFEAST INVOKE WENDIGOCOMMANDS~
Wendigo command gifts:
  1 CAMOUFLAGE: invokes the native hiding effect.
  2 CUTTING <target>: native Cutting Wind attack.
  3 BLOODYFEAST <corpse>: consumes eligible remains for a temporary
    damage-roll affect; it does not permanently raise base stats.
  5 INVOKE FOG or INVOKE RAIN: outdoor weather toggles.
    INVOKE LIGHTNING <target>: native lightning attack.
Invoke retains its weather cooldown and outdoor requirements.
Related: WENDIGOS, WWGIFTS, WWUPKEEP.
~

